<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annaly</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anghaile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Annaly was a medieval Irish lordship in the northern part of Tethba, roughly the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-longford">County Longford</a>. From the 11th and 12th centuries it was ruled by the Uí Fergail, later known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ofarrell">O'Farrells</a>, who kept it largely free of the Anglo-Norman lords of Meath. It was made into County Longford in the late 16th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/annaly.jpg" alt="Annaly" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oxenhillshaw · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Baron_Annaly.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
